%% Lambda SQS Integration
%% Shows auto-triggered pymysql consumer (sqs-consumer-orm is manual only)

sequenceDiagram
    participant Producer as sqs-producer Lambda
    participant SQS as SQS Queue
    participant Consumer as sqs-consumer Lambda<br/>(pymysql)
    participant RDS as MySQL Database

    Note over Producer,RDS: Auto-triggered Message Flow (pymysql)

    Producer->>SQS: SendMessage<br/>{name, description, price, quantity}

    Note over SQS: Message in queue<br/>Visibility: 60s<br/>Retention: 24h

    SQS->>Consumer: Event Source Mapping<br/>Triggers (batch up to 10)

    loop For each record in batch
        Consumer->>Consumer: Parse message.body (JSON)
        Consumer->>RDS: pymysql: INSERT INTO items (...)
        alt Success
            RDS-->>Consumer: OK
            Note over Consumer: Message auto-deleted
        else Failure
            Consumer-->>SQS: Throw error
            Note over SQS: Retry (up to 3x)
        end
    end

    Note over SQS: After 3 failures → DLQ

    Note over Producer,RDS: Alternative: sqs-consumer-orm<br/>Uses SQLAlchemy ORM<br/>Manual invocation only (no event source)
